 "notes": "Extra clips: swim-left, swim-down, swim-up (head and the back's hump above water) and soak-down (sitting in water, content closed eyes): the waterline is the body's last row, lapped by light ripples (\"water\") at irregular columns that run 1 px past each flank, with ripple arcs under the flanks, one foam speck (\"foam\") and a dark reflection line (\"water.dark\") 1 row under the body; there is no water fill, so the lake shows through. swim-left has a bow wave at the snout. The runtime should hide the shadow. loaf-down (lying as a loaf, muzzle on the floor, eyes shut), blink-down. sleep-any is the side profile lying flat with the muzzle on the floor. groom-left stands and lifts the near foreleg: the paw comes up in front of the chest, to the muzzle (tongue out) and to the cheek. pounce-left is a small hop. stretch-left, pounce-left and yawn-down are one-shots.",
